														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3698741">
									

<p>This skip is basically Mr. Hax in terms of its concept, which is that ultimately, the created hates its creator, and struggles to deal with that. Hax bogs itself down in its anomaly (more impressive than this one yet still not really playing into the concept or character much) and follow-through (Hax’s feelings and motivations felt muddied and confusing, but had actual emotional weight). I get not every anomaly is gonna like existing, but they have to be interesting.</p>
<p>And yes, this is compared to Hax because it follows almost the exact same beats and doesn’t improve on that article at all. Your follow-through ends with “mad about existing” (incidentially, my favorite Mister), and also this guy’s existance is a living Hell, so I guess I’m sad for him. This doesn’t have any character traits or personality pieces I remember at all after finishing, whereas I can at least remember with Hax that it felt super bitter but still sorrowful and wistful. This? He’s just mad because he’s angry.</p>
<p>So it's a good skip for people who don't like the group, but it's not actually a good skip.</p>

							</div>

								
